  "body": "# SongCore #172 — S3 Linux reference evidence: FINAL MERGED CLOSEOUT\n\n> **Final authoritative PR metadata (2026-10-29).** **MERGED** by squash into `main` as `b49b18cd68ae1a353cd3396efb3977b8590cc4d1`; reviewed source head `2882e486a56d0b68f07da55f3189c548895021a0`; previous main base `742abf87ef2a832b653b17760d8c2a55008cb1c1`. **This is an S3 engineering-evidence integration, not SongCore RELEASE.** Issues #172, #329 and #330 remain OPEN pending their independent gates.\n\n## 1. Final change set — CLEAN DELTA\n\n| Dimension | Final outcome |\n|---|---|\n| PR | #328 MERGED, squash `b49b18cd68ae1a353cd3396efb3977b8590cc4d1` |\n| Final reviewed HEAD | `2882e486a56d0b68f07da55f3189c548895021a0` |\n| PR changed files | **90**, all additions: **89 `evidence/**` + 1 `ops/build-linux.sh`** |\n| Product code | **0 changed files**; no mutation/deletion; no inherited PR-A/B changes |\n| History | Restacked branch **1 commit ahead of previous main**, replacing the earlier erroneous 562-file stacked comparison |\n| Main | `ops/build-linux.sh` and 727-line append-only `ERRATUM-20261029.md` present on merged main |\n\nThe previous body described historical heads `268f338`, `ee1de95`, `2af010ea` and 561/562-file ancestral diffs; those snapshots are **not the merged PR's state**. The source-equivalence and clean-delta audit was independently completed before merge. No need to retain inaccurate ancestor changes to cause GitHub Actions path filters to match.\n\n## 2. Additive evidence correction — historical records preserved\n\n**[ERRATUM-20261029.md (merged main)](https://github.com/jnhu76/qianqian/blob/b49b18cd68ae1a353cd3396efb3977b8590cc4d1/evidence/songcore-172/linux/verify/canonical/ERRATUM-20261029.md)**\n\n- The erratum records eight record/provenance findings and later external-consumer corroboration. Original `s3-build.md`, `s3-verify.md`, `c-suite-receipt.json`, `external-consumer-receipt.txt`, raw failed-gate logs and old hashes were **not overwritten**. The 55/55 textual claim was corrected by additive evidence: **57/57** build-manifest hashes; distinct verify manifest **26/26**.\n- Historical C-suite `suite_sources` lacks executed source bytes/hashes and refers to `ops/verify-suite/...` paths that were not committed there; **historical executed-source == archived-source remains NOT_ESTABLISHED**. Current-day validations do not backfill earlier missing execution receipts.\n- The genuine `run1-derive` compile is distinguished from later `clone=reuse` / `closure=reuse` cache re-entry. Re-entry PASS is **not** two fresh builds or L1 fresh-closure proof.\n- Appended **C.1–C.6** disambiguates duplicate A.6 headings, old versus later E14 execution snapshots, and the clean-delta versus GitHub Actions trigger distinction. **C.4** narrows the historical “cannot both hold” phrase: clean ancestry may coexist with **new** explicit `workflow_dispatch` E01–E18 PASS.\n- Two **nonblocking archival phrasing debts** are recorded, not silently changed: old A.6 lines approximately 629–638 speak in present tense about ancestral `native/**` files and predict E14 NOT_RUN, but **are false for the final clean head**; interpret those lines as historical observations only under Appendix C and GitHub current facts. C.3 also uses shortened `5b26c74` for a superseded, now-unreachable head; its run identity must be checked via GitHub workflow `head_sha`, never from reachability of that short ref. Those debts do not change final verified results and were judged nonblocking, not rewritten in archival text.\n\n## 3. External consumer — NEW corroborating execution, not retroactive proof\n\nThe original five-line external-consumer receipt is not direct proof of historical run commands or exit codes. The new evidence appendix records later actual WSL2 unpacked-tarball consumer execution for **both Linux static and shared**:\n- Archive `d33f6762…97fcbe`, 2,593,935 bytes, `metadata/checksums.txt` **14/14 PASS**.\n- C consumer SHA `d1454731…`, header `cf509a5c…`, static lib `409ef3da…`, shared `5e9c5697…`, FLAC sample `d8062668…`; full hashes and argv in the erratum.\n- Static and shared: compiler and runtime exit codes all **0**; identical seven-line real decode output SHA256 `ebe7254319fddc5d5fc03fac043c3f37744bb60672d1ffccfc689fa4d9071fdf`, including **176400 frames**, seek **1985306 μs**, and clean EOF.\n- This is *newly earned* package-consumption corroboration, **not** missing proof for the original §4 run, an independent new source closure, L1/L2/L3, or proof of an earlier suite's byte identity.\n\n## 4. Final HEAD release controls — explicit run, no false CI trigger\n\n**[Qianqian Release run 40888616589](https://github.com/jnhu76/qianqian/actions/runs/40888616589)** at exact head `2882e486a56d0b68f07da55f3189c548895021a0`:\n- `event=workflow_dispatch` on **the clean final PR branch/head**, not a `pull_request.paths` false positive from stacked history.\n- Build job **SUCCESS**, step `Release adversarial controls (E01–E18)` **completed / SUCCESS**.\n- Publish job **SKIPPED**; no tag or GitHub release.\n- No `native/**` or `crates/**` file is changed by this PR. Its actual `evidence/**` and `ops/**` delta need not trigger the Release PR workflow by path; an explicit dispatch supplies **final-head-specific** evidence instead.\n\nA Windows-local historical E14 RED is still an actual host-specific failure, **not** erased by this Linux CI E01–E18 PASS. E14 cross-host remediation is separately owned by #330. Full local `lefthook run pre-push --all-files` was **not executed** in the final independent check; the independent reviewer did execute two always-on Python checks successfully on the archived snapshot, and separate local gate receipts were reported. Do not elevate this to a full pre-push PASS.\n\n## 5. Independent review and bounded merge decision\n\nThe final head received independent **APPROVE** after clean-delta, archive-hash, additive-erratum, final-head workflow and PR-record review, then was **squash-merged**. Merge SHA `b49b18cd68ae1a353cd3396efb3977b8590cc4d1` is the source of truth for main integration; no further merge action is pending for #328.\n\nThe following remain **outside #328** and are not implicitly passed or promoted by its merge:\n\n- **#329:** FFmpeg archive cross-root ordinary-section path leakage (8 members, plus correct duplicate-member comparison), one-factor E0/E1/E2 flags, fresh L1, true G2-on-R2 / L2 and shipped-library byte reproducibility / L3.\n- **#330:** E14 Windows/Linux gate governance, real docs-verify, S1 authority ratification, three source/spec differentials and AGENTS gate routing.\n- **#172:** G4/Owner release decision, 6×2 final release matrix, support maturity and version/publisher reservations.\n\n**Historical Windows RC frozen SHA256:** `7b4d0615d25af464739373a0a3565f77f3208ce9c263f59e578d443801536415`. No `songcore-v*` tag, GitHub Release or Windows SUPPORTED promotion in this PR.\n\n**FINAL:** `PR_328=MERGED; MERGE_SHA=b49b18cd68ae1a353cd3396efb3977b8590cc4d1; DIFF=90_ADDED_ONLY; PRODUCT_CODE_DELTA=0; FINAL_HEAD_E01_E18=PASS_VIA_WORKFLOW_DISPATCH; PUBLISH=SKIPPED; SONGCORE_RELEASE=BLOCKED_UNTIL_172_G4`.\n",
